#	Pattern	Typical clues
1	Basic Traversal	Find max/min/sum/count, process every element
2	Hash Map / Hash Set	Frequency, duplicates, "have I seen this?", complement
3	Two Pointers	Sorted array, pair problems, compare from both ends
4	Sliding Window	Contiguous subarray/substring, longest/shortest, fixed/variable window
5	Prefix Sum	Repeated range sums, subarray sum
6	Binary Search	Sorted data, search efficiently, "minimum/maximum possible answer"
7	Sorting + Greedy	Sort first, then make locally optimal choices
8	Intervals	[start, end], overlapping intervals, scheduling
9	Stack / Monotonic Stack	Matching brackets, next greater/smaller, previous greater/smaller
10	Queue / Deque	Process in order, BFS, sliding-window maximum
11	Linked List Techniques	Fast/slow pointers, reversal, cycle detection
12	Tree DFS	Recursive tree traversal, depth, paths
13	Tree BFS	Level-order traversal, shortest level distance
14	Heap / Priority Queue	Top K, smallest/largest, continuously get min/max
15	Graph DFS/BFS	Connectivity, paths, components, islands
16	Topological Sort	Dependencies, prerequisites, ordering
17	Union-Find / DSU	Connected components, grouping, dynamic connectivity
18	Backtracking	Generate all combinations/permutations/subsets
19	Greedy	Make the best local decision at each step
20	Dynamic Programming	Number of ways, optimal result, overlapping subproblems
21	Memoization	Recursion + cache previously calculated states
22	Trie	Prefix/search problems involving words
23	Bit Manipulation	XOR, binary representation, bit-based tricks
24	Advanced Graph Algorithms	Dijkstra, MST, shortest paths
25	Advanced DP	2D DP, subsequence DP, knapsack, state-machine DP
